creted urokinase (PLAU) and neuropilin 1 (NRP1) on pancreatic cancer-associated fibroblasts. This approach is thus useful for systematic exploring new ligand-receptor pairs and discovering critical intercellular signaling events.\n\n[METHODS]\nCell Lysis and Pull-Down. After washed with PBS three times, cells were lysed with lysis buffer containing 2% Triton X-100, 150 mM HEPES pH 8.2, 1.5 mM EDTA, 60 mM 2-chloroacetamide, 1 mM phenylmethanesulfonylfluoride, 5 μg/mL aprotinin (Amresco), 5 μg/mL pepstatin (Amresco) and 50 U/mL non-restriction nucleases (Beyotime). The lysate was centrifuged at 14,000g, 4 °C for 6 min, and the resulting supernatant was transferred to a new tube. Streptavidin beads (Thermo Scientific; 1 μL bead volume for 106 cells) were added to the supernatant, and samples were placed on an end-over-end rotator for overnight at 4 °C. Beads were then transferred to spin column and washed three times with washing buffer (6 M urea, 1% SDS, 50 mM Tris-HCl, pH 7.4) and once with 1.5 M NaCl. Then the beads were incubated in alkylation buffer (5 mM TCEP, 50 mM 2-chloroacetamide, 0.2 M ammonium bicarbonate, and 0.5 M NaCl) at 37 °C for 60 min and wash three times with 20% ethanol to completely remove detergents. The purified proteins on beads were digested with 8 ng/μL Trypsin (Promega) and 1.6 ng/μL Lys-C (Wako) in 50 mM ammonium bicarbonate at 37 °C overnight on an end-over-end rotator. Digestion mixtures were acidified to pH <3 using trifluoroacetic acid (TFA), desalted with StageTips, and lyophilized. LC-MS/MS Analysis. Peptide samples were dissolved in a solution of 5% ACN and 4% FA. The resulting samples were analyzed by a nano-flow liquid chromatography coupled to a Thermo Fisher Orbitrap Q Exactive, Q Exactive HF-X, Orbitrap Fusion or Bruker timsTOF Pro mass spectrometer. Detailed instrument settings can be found in SI Appendix, Supplemental Methods.\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17', 'store': True, 'temperature': 0.3}}
